==Battleground==
*20 [[Those Guys]] spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*10 [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 6 seconds<sup>180f</sup>, delay 4~8 seconds<sup>120f~240f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 8~16 seconds<sup>240f~480f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bearkini]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 2~10 seconds<sup>60f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Send out your meatshields, and then [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]]. If you have any strong cats, use them too, including [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]. When Bearkini appears, spam your cats to take her out. Once Bearkini is dead, proceed to destroy the enemy base.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Never Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Summer!]] stages, Something About Cats' Japanese name, Neko ni Matsuwaru Et Cetera, references a song, in this case "[https://youtu.be/tht0SnekaLM Nagisa ni Matsuwaru Et Cetera]" by [[wikipedia:PuffyAyumi|PuffyAyumi]].

